.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-3-Clause
.Dd October 23, 2026
.Dt WSCONSCTL 8
.Os OxideBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm wsconsctl
.Nd show and set the console's settings
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl n
.Op Fl a | Ar name ...
.Nm
.Op Fl n
.Ar name Ns = Ns Ar value ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
shows or changes the settings of the system console.
With a
.Ar name
it prints
.Ar name Ns = Ns Ar value ;
with
.Ar name Ns = Ns Ar value
it changes the setting, which only root may do, and prints
.Ar name Li -> Ar value .
With no operand, or
.Fl a ,
it prints every setting.
.Fl n
prints values alone.
.Pp
The settings are:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Va keyboard.encoding
The keyboard's layout, for PS/2 and USB keyboards alike:
.Bl -tag -width us.colemak -compact
.It Li us
US English (the default)
.It Li uk
UK English
.It Li de
German
.It Li fr
French AZERTY
.It Li us.dvorak
Dvorak
.It Li us.colemak
Colemak
.It Li jp
Japanese 109-key
.It Li no
Norwegian
.It Li fi , Li sv
Finnish and Swedish
.El
Keys held down when the layout changes are forgotten.
The console terminal receives what the keys type as UTF-8, and shows the
characters its font has; the rest it shows as
.Ql \(sq .
.It Va display.palette
The console's 16 colours:
.Bl -tag -width us.colemak -compact
.It Li vga
the standard VGA colours (the default)
.It Li rust
OxideBSD's own: each colour's hue kept, in oxidised metal (rust for brown and
red, verdigris and patina for cyan and green, brass for yellow, steel for blue)
on a warm black and cream
.El
A program may also redefine colours itself with the Linux console's
.Li ESC ] P Ar nrrggbb
(as
.Xr ncurses 3 Ns 's
.Fn init_color
does with the
.Li linux
terminal type);
.Li ESC ] R
puts back the palette's own.
.El
.Pp
.Pa /etc/rc.d/wsconsctl
applies
.Xr wsconsctl.conf 5
at boot.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width /etc/wsconsctl.conf -compact
.It Pa /dev/ttyv0
the console, whose requests these are
.It Pa /etc/wsconsctl.conf
the settings made at boot
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
0 if every setting was shown or set, 1 otherwise.
.Sh EXAMPLES
A German keyboard:
.Dl wsconsctl keyboard.encoding=de
.Pp
The rust colours:
.Dl wsconsctl display.palette=rust
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr wsconsctl.conf 5
.Sh HISTORY
A
.Nm
command first appeared in
.Nx 1.4 .
OxideBSD's takes NetBSD's and OpenBSD's names for the settings it has.
